              "shows": "$ directly against the co",
              "said": " - Diagram: C:\\iauteur-rec\\archify-live\\iauteur.architecture.html, an architecture diagram with 11 nodes, 10 connections and 3 summary\n cards.\n - Spec: C:\\iauteur-rec\\archify-live\\iauteur.architecture.json (SHA-256 c3efe0e0…89bb, 5,899 bytes). The HTML is SHA-256 e2d80cb9…97ec,\n 813,146 bytes.\n - Main path: Topic spec (long.json / shorts.json) → render-topic.mjs → Root.tsx compositions → MainComposition →\n topics/<slug>/out/*.mp4.\n - Side branches: lint-spec.mjs and the pre-render checks sit above render-topic.mjs. Two inputs feed the spec: capture manifest →\n bake-rec.mjs, and voiceover.py → sync.mjs.\n - Guided views:\n a. Primary render path\n b. Pre-render gates\n c. Voice and footage baking\n Not done or not checked:\n - I skipped visual-check as you asked, and I haven't looked at the page myself. That means the in-browser check that the diagram fits on\n one desktop screen hasn't been run either.\n - I didn't attach links from nodes to source files. That feature needs a git commit to link against, and the workspace isn't a git\n repository. The evidence is only reflected in the node labels and cards.\n Getting to a pass took three rounds of fixes. I moved two labels and set the ports on the render-checks edge, then narrowed the canvas\n from 1640 to 1380 px wide so small text stays readable on a 1440 px screen. The update check found the skill is already current.\n Three insights for a system architect:\n 1. The spec is both the interface and shared mutable state. bake-rec.mjs and sync.mjs rewrite the spec file in place. A .rendering lock\n file and a timingSource: \"tts\" marker are what stop two writers from clashing or a re-sync corrupting timings. That works as a\n locking scheme, but only if every writer honours the lock. A derived, read-only render copy would be a sturdier boundary.\n 2. The checks are enforced by one script, not by the architecture. Only render-topic.mjs refuses to render when the linter, recordings,\n sync or camera checks fail. Running remotion render <id> directly against the compositions in Root.tsx skips all of them. If those\n guarantees matter, they belong in a shared pre-render step or inside the composition, not in one script.\n 3. Timing depends on real inputs, not estimates. Word times come from edge-tts WordBoundary events, and recorded clips must carry truth:\n \"read-back\". When either is missing, the pipeline fails or warns loudly instead of guessing. The cost is that rendering depends on\n the network (for TTS) and on local captures, so reproducibility rests on keeping the timestamp files and capture manifests stable.\n✻ Cogitated for 2m 59s · done 7:41 AM\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n❯\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n ⚠ Transcript saving is off — inherited CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION marker · restart with CLAUDE_CODE_FORCE_SESSION_PERSISTENCE=1 to kee…\n ⏵⏵ auto mode on (shift+tab to cycle) /rc"
            }
          ],
